Kvmd errors, timeouts, and retry
---------------------------------

Typed HTTP failure (a status on the error) and one retry of
GET /streamer/snapshot after HTTP 503 are adapted from
dvaerum/pikvm_mcp_server (https://github.com/dvaerum/pikvm_mcp_server)
src/pikvm/client.ts PiKVMApiError and fetchSnapshotWithRetry at
b5fdc31e16525f196282436a0fa7ca797eea2e5e (GPL-3.0). The grace period is
1500 ms. Together with the 3-attempt GET schedule, a snapshot makes at
most 4 calls. This fork does not take the websocket keepalive from that
commit.

AbortSignal.timeout, PIKVM_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS (default 5000), and the
no-retry codes PIKVM_UNREACHABLE and PIKVM_AUTH_FAILED are adapted from
dtrukr/pikvm_mcp_server (https://github.com/dtrukr/pikvm_mcp_server)
src/pikvm/client.ts and src/config.ts at
d120243c4b81802ae725c18b39c4681ce89bfb7a (GPL-3.0). A timeout is reported
as PIKVM_TIMEOUT. Idempotent GET retry is local to this fork: 3
attempts, sleeping 250 ms then 500 ms plus jitter, on network errors,
timeouts, HTTP 502, and HTTP 503. POST is not retried. HTTP 400, 401,
403, 409, 500, and 504 are not retried. The snapshot 503 grace retry
is in addition to those 3 attempts, so GET /streamer/snapshot makes at
most 4 calls. POST /hid/* is not aborted by the ordinary deadline.

